  INFORMATION CONTENT PER WALSH ORDER:
  (How many bits of information about T does each order carry?)

  Order 2: 92.3% of Var(H), 105 coefficients, 1.285714 per coeff
  Order 4: 7.7% of Var(H), 1365 coefficients, 0.008242 per coeff

  KEY INSIGHT: Order 2 = PAIRWISE arc interactions dominate.
  This is WHY the score sequence (which captures marginal
  arc behavior) explains 97% of H variation (the OCR).
  The remaining 3% comes from order-4 and higher interactions.
  ODD orders are EXACTLY ZERO -- H is complement-invariant
  (flipping all arcs preserves H, by path-reversal symmetry).
